    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0134" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg42"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/8648</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-25T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 25, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1382. I have just seen a copy of the secret treaty, April 25 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">26</hi>], 1915, between Italy, France, England and
                    Russia; presume that you <pb facs="0135" n="43" xml:id="pg43"/> have seen it as
                    it appeared in Russia<anchor n="1" xml:id="d27-f1"/> and in the English magazine
                        <hi rendition="#italic">New Europe</hi>. It has not been published in Italy
                    nor, I believe, in France. Prime Minister Orlando has gone to England accompanied by Minister of War and
                        Crespi, Food Commissioner to Paris, to seek a
                    reaffirmation of this secret treaty in view of the speeches by the President and
                        Lloyd George. It is reported that
                        Orlando and Sonnino had a stiff quarrel; the latter refused
                    to go to England saying that he had the Allies’ written promise and he was
                    against discussing the matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
